{"seconds": 225.6, "exit": 0, "final": "Let me just note the FEN needs fixing (I'm missing a square). After **Ne7+ Kg7**, White can play **Nxc2** or **Rxc2**, and Black plays **Bxc1**, winning the rook. So the main tactical blow is:\n\n**1...Bd2!** (attacking the rook and pawn e3)\n- If **2.Nxc2 Bxc1+** or **2.Rxc2 Bxc2**, Black wins the rook\n- If **2.Ne7+ Kg7**, then White still cannot save both the c2 pawn and the rook\n\nSo **Bd2** is the clearly best move! It's a decoy/removal sacrifice that forces White to lose the rook.\n\n**Best move: Bd2**\n**Main line: Bd2 Nxc2 Bxc1+ and Black wins the rook**\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Bd2\", \"line\": [\"Bd2\", \"Nxc2\", \"Bxc1+\", \"Kxc1\", \"Bxe3\"], \"motifs\": [\"deflection\", \"capturingDefender\", \"fork\"]}\n```\n\n**Coaching note:** The key is recognizing that the rook on c1 is overloaded\u2014it both defends the pawn on c2 AND guards against promotion. Attacking it with **Bd2** removes the defender because any way White captures your c2 pawn, the rook becomes undefended and you win it outright. This is a classic \"deflection\"\u2014forcing the defender to abandon its duty.", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r5k1/8/6P1/5N2/1b1Np3/3bP3/PKp2P2/2R5 b - - 1 42"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r5k1/8/6P1/5N2/1b1Np3/3bP3/PKp2P2/2R5 b - - 1 42"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5k1/8/6P1/5N2/1b1Np3/3bP3/PKp2P2/2R5 b - - 1 42", "move": "Bb1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5k1/8/6P1/5N2/1b1Np3/3bP3/PKp2P2/2R5 b - - 1 42", "move": "Ba1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5k1/8/6P1/5N2/1b1Np3/3bP3/PKp2P2/2R5 b - - 1 42", "move": "Bc3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5k1/8/6P1/5N2/3Np3/2bbP3/PKp2P2/2R5 w - - 2 43", "move": "Kb3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5k1/8/6P1/5N2/3Np3/1KbbP3/P1p2P2/2R5 b - - 3 43", "